'''Keyan Farlander''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] who served as a [[rebel pilot]] within the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].<ref name="Starfighter Missions" /> Farlander was present at a briefing aboard the Alliance [[flagship]] ''[[Home One]]'' shortly prior to the [[Battle of Endor]]. During the briefing he stood beside [[Palso Thern]] and other fellow pilots.<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref>

As an [[A/SF-01 B-wing starfighter]] [[pilot]], Farlander was equipped with a [[Color|red]] [[flight suit]] and [[helmet]]. He had light skin and brown [[hair]].<ref name="Starfighter Missions" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Keyan Farlander first appeared as the player character in the [[Star Wars Legends|Legends]] video game [[Star Wars: X-Wing (video game)|''Star Wars: X-Wing'']], with a history expanded on in the game's supplemental material. Sources published in the many years following the game's release would identify Farlander as the pilot of the [[BTL-A4 Y-wing assault starfighter/bomber|Y-wing]] seen flying away from the exploding [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station/Legends|Death Star]] alongside the ''[[Millennium Falcon/Legends|Millennium Falcon]]'' and [[Luke Skywalker/Legends|Luke Skywalker]] and [[Wedge Antilles/Legends|Wedge Antilles]]' [[T-65B X-wing starfighter|X-wings]] in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].<ref name="Insider63">{{InsiderCite|63|Star Wars Q&A|''Star Wars'' Q&A}}</ref> In the new [[canon]] started in [[2014]], the identity of the Y-wing pilot was changed to [[Evaan Verlaine]], who also had a different callsign (Gold Three).<ref name="SWGA">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> The identity of Gold Seven was changed to [[Gazdo Woolcob]].<ref name="Grounded">{{StoryCite|story=Grounded|book=From a Certain Point of View}}</ref>

